[38;2;124;124;124mActually, let me reconsider the precise statement. The question: "Do Gromov-[0m
[38;2;124;124;124mWitten invariants count the morphisms from a curve to a variety over $[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m\mathbb{C}$?"[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mThe answer is no. Let me give the reasons:[0m

[38;2;124;124;124m1. **Domain**: GW invariants involve stable maps from prestable (nodal) curves, [0m[38;2;124;124;124mnot just morphisms from a single (smooth) curve.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124m2. **Virtual nature**: The invariant is defined via virtual fundamental class, [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mso it's a virtual count. When the moduli space is obstructed, the "count" [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mdoesn't correspond to actual geometric objects.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124m3. **Automorphism weighting**: The count is weighted by $1/|\text{Aut}(f)|$, [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mgiving rational numbers, not integer counts.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124m4. **Multiple covers**: A single image curve can be covered by maps of higher [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mdegree, and these contribute to the invariant.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124m5. **Even in genus 0 with 3 points on $\mathbb{P}^1$ target**: The moduli $[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m\overline{M}_{0,0}(\mathbb{P}^2, d)$ has boundary strata corresponding to [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mreducible domains, so the "count" includes maps from nodal curves.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mSo the proof is essentially: GW invariants are defined as integrals over the [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mmoduli space of stable maps against the virtual fundamental class. This is a [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mvirtual count that:[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m- allows nodal domain curves (not just smooth curves)[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m- weights by automorphisms (rational, not integer)[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m- uses virtual fundamental class (counts even when obstructed)[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m- includes multiple cover contributions[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mTherefore they do not, in general, count morphisms from a curve to a variety.[0m

